`VisibilityCondition.value` is typed as `any`. To keep downstream code type-safe, prefer `unknown` (with narrowing) or a constrained JSON value type (e.g., `string | number | boolean | null | ...`) instead of `any`.
```suggestion
export type VisibilityPrimitive = string | number | boolean | null;

export type VisibilityValue = VisibilityPrimitive | VisibilityPrimitive[];

export type VisibilityCondition = {
  field: string;
  operator?: '=' | '!=' | '>' | '>=' | '<' | '<=' | 'in';
  value?: VisibilityValue;
```

`fetchData` returns early when `dataSource` is missing, without setting an error or clearing the loading state. In remote mode this can leave the component in an infinite loading state. Consider setting `error` and `loading=false` when `!hasInlineData && !dataSource`.
```suggestion
    if (hasInlineData) return;
    if (!dataSource) {
      setError(new Error('DataSource required'));
      setLoading(false);
      return;
    }
```

`TextCellRenderer` uses `value || '-'`, which will incorrectly render `0` (and other falsy-but-valid values) as `'-'`. Prefer a nullish/empty-string check (e.g., `value == null || value === ''`).
```suggestion
  const displayValue = value == null || value === '' ? '-' : value;
  return <span className="truncate">{displayValue}</span>;
```

